{
  "dom_id": "step-q276481",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $5+10+20+\u22ef?$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=2.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-5(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =5({2}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
